{"Name": "document6", "Natural": "Here is a 2-3 sentence summary of the text:\n\nBeverage companies spent $866 million on advertising unhealthy drinks in 2013, and the government is considering a ban on sugary drinks to combat obesity. However, opponents argue that people need to take responsibility for their own health and that a ban would not be effective in reducing obesity rates. Additionally, there are other factors that contribute to obesity, such as genetics and processed foods, and a ban on sugary drinks would not address these underlying issues."}
{"Name": "document2", "Natural": "Here is a summary of the text in 2-3 sentences:\n\nThe sugary drinks portion cap rule, also known as the soda ban, was a proposed limit on soft drink size in New York City, intended to prohibit the sale of sweetened drinks larger than 16 fluid ounces. The rule was strongly supported by Mayor Michael Bloomberg and his successor, Mayor Bill de Blasio, but was opposed by beverage companies and some community groups. The rule was ultimately repealed by the New York Court of Appeals in 2014, citing that the New York City Board of Health exceeded its regulatory authority."}

